feat(harbormaster): implement canonical merge-owning actor body (ADR-0037)

Harbormaster is the canonical actor that owns merges of operator-accepted
dispatches. The body polls the merge_queue every 30s (or reacts to a
dispatch:accepted channel event), rebases each accepted dispatch's worktree
onto origin/main, and runs `gh pr merge` with the per-dispatch merge style.

Two-key safety, enforced in code rather than policy:
  - dispatches.state = 'accepted'  AND
  - merge_queue.state = 'queued'
Either key missing, the row is skipped. dispatch_id IS NULL (operator-authored
PR) is out of scope per ADR-0037 Scope narrowing.

What the harbormaster will never do:
  - bypass the pd-shim git wrapper (PR #161) -- all destructive verbs flow
    through ~/.port-daddy/bin/git and PD_SHIM_OFF is explicitly stripped
    from the runner env
  - auto-merge to main without operator-approved dispatch state
  - run two merges against the same base_branch concurrently
    (per-base in-process lock)
  - pretend a merge happened -- gh non-zero exit marks state='blocked' and
    posts a pd note to operator, never silent retry

Conflict path: detected via git status --porcelain after a rebase failure,
the rebase is aborted, the dispatch is moved back to 'produced' with an
error_message, the merge_queue row is blocked, and a pd note is posted to
the worker actor's mailbox with the goal text a future sub-dispatch will
inherit (ADR-0035 parent_dispatch_id when that schema lands).

Files:
  - migrations/084_harbormaster_actor.sql -- idempotent canonical actor row
    with caps merge:approve, merge:execute, merge:queue-manage,
    conflict:resolve, gh:write
  - lib/harbormaster.ts -- body (start/stop/tick/processCandidate)
    with file-lease, CommandRunner injection, and graceful no-op when
    PR #163 dispatches/merge_queue schema additions are not yet present
  - cli/commands/harbormaster.ts -- pd harbormaster start|stop|status|queue
  - fleet/harbormaster.yml -- fleet ship snippet (triggers: cron every-30s +
    channel dispatch:accepted; backend cli:claude-code; allowedTools
    Bash(git*|gh*|pd note*|pd dispatch*))
  - tests/unit/harbormaster.test.js -- 17 tests covering migration
    idempotency, two-key constraint, rebase success/conflict/blocked
    paths, merge-style routing, base_branch lock, file lease
  - completions + features.manifest.json -- wired pd harbormaster + hm
    alias across bash/zsh/fish

Validation: 5840 unit tests pass; tsc clean; merge-queue suite (44/44)
still green. Body is dormant until migrations 082 (actors table) and
083 (dispatches table) + a merge_queue dispatch_id/state-column upgrade
all land -- findCandidates() returns [] and emits only tick events.


